From: DaffyDabz <daffydabz@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 09:25:57 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 344/371] family server: a ship that is out when its pirate
 re-logs from the pirate chooser keeps its steering wheel

A pirate who went back to the pirate chooser with his ship out and picked the same pirate had the ship loader
activate the ship (and its hull and masts) a second time. The database state server ignores an activate for an
object that is already active, but AstronInternalRepository.sendActivate chases an activate-with-fields with a
SET_LOCATION(0, 0); the state server's move to parent 0 set the ship's AI channel to 0 without a CHANGING_AI, so
the AI only logged 'setLocation 0 0' and kept a dead PlayerShipAI. The next launch reused it (ENTER_AI ignored,
'already know') and the ship had no wheel (claude2, ship 100000750, 09:00:34 and 04:02:33; the same as games'
04:07 LIVE-upgrade no-wheel).

ActivateShipFSM now asks getActivated first (activateUnlessUp): a ship or part that is still up is not activated
again; the owner steps (setOwnerAgain + post-remove) run after in both cases. Offline sim of the state server
rules with the loader's real steps (places' sim_ship_reactivate.py): HEAD FAIL (AI dropped from the ship and both
parts, ship moved to 0,0), patched PASS (re-login keeps ship + AI with the owner back; a fresh login activates and
owns as before). UberDOG only. A ship already left as a dead copy on the AI clears at the next real logout or AI
restart.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
